# Local repository rules for this workspace

1) Follow the project's formal coding rules
   - Always follow RULES_coding.md and RULES_ports.md. These documents define mandatory coding, testing and port rules for this codebase.

2) Documentation must be kept up-to-date
   - Any change that affects behavior, deployment, or architecture must be reflected in docs/*.md before merging.
   - At minimum update README.md (run/start instructions), ARCHITECTURE.md (design changes) and docs/IMPLEMENTATIONPLAN.md (see below) when appropriate.

3) Implementation plan required for non-trivial changes
   - Before making "big changes" (feature additions, refactors, infra changes), create or update docs/IMPLEMENTATIONPLAN.md.
   - The implementation plan must contain: task description, concrete action steps, files to change, testing plan, rollback plan and expected time estimate.
   - Only after the plan is reviewed (by the maintainer or an assigned reviewer) proceed with implementation.

4) Tests and validation
   - Run unit tests and linters locally before committing. Add tests for new behavior.
   - If the change touches backend or packaging, run the full integration checklist in docs/DOCKER.md (if applicable).

5) Changelog and release notes
   - Add a short entry to docs/CHANGELOG.md for user-facing or breaking changes.

6) Small housekeeping
   - Keep commits focused and well-described. Use imperative commit messages.
   - Remove debug code and console.log/print statements prior to commit.

7) If in doubt
   - Open a short draft PR or ping the maintainer. Use the repository /reportbug command for urgent issues.

This file is intentionally concise — authoring and review should continue in docs/IMPLEMENTATIONPLAN.md for any substantial work.